15, 12-12·9/25, 9-9·9/25) = (15, 12·16/25, 144/25) = (15, 192/25, 144/25).\n\nNow G = intersection of DF and BE.\n\nD=(0,12,0), F=(135/34, 0, 225/34). Line DF: D + s(F-D) = (135s/34, 12-12s, 225s/34).\nB=(15,0,0), E=(0, 108/25, 144/25). Line BE: B + u(E-B) = (15-15u, 108u/25, 144u/25).\n\nSet equal:\n135s/34 = 15-15u  ... (1)\n12-12s = 108u/25   ... (2)\n225s/34 = 144u/25  ... (3)\n\nFrom (3): s = 144u·34/(25·225) = 144·34 u / 5625 = 4896u/5625. Simplify: 4896/5625. GCD... 4896 = 16·306 = 16·306. 5625=9·625=9·625. GCD(4896,5625): 4896=2^4·3·102=2^4·3·2·51=2^5·3·51=2^5·3^2·17. 5625=3^2·5^4... wait 5625=625·9=5^4·3^2. So GCD=3^2=9. s = 544u/625.\n\nFrom (2): 12-12s = 108u/25 → 12(1-s) = 108u/25 → 1-s = 9u/25 → s = 1-9u/25.\n\nSet equal: 544u/625 = 1-9u/25 = 1 - 225u/625. So 544u/625 + 225u/625 = 1 → 769u/625 = 1 → u = 625/769.\n\ns = 544·625/(625·769) = 544/769.\n\nCheck (1): 135s/34 = 135·544/(34·769) = 73440/(26146). 15-15u = 15(1-625/769) = 15·144/769 = 2160/769. Left: 135·544/(34·769) = 73440/(34·769) = 2160/769. ✓ (73440/34 = 2160). \n\nSo G: using DF: x = 135s/34 = 135·544/(34·769) = 2160/769. y = 12-12s = 12(1-544/769) = 12·225/769 = 2700/769. z = 225s/34 = 225·544/(34·769) = 122400/(34·769) = 3600/769.\n\nG = (2160/769, 2700/769, 3600/769).\n\nNow P = intersection of DN and BM.\n\nD=(0,12,0), N=(15, 192/25, 144/25). Line DN: D + s'(N-D) = (15s', 12 + s'(192/25-12), s'·144/25). 192/25-12 = 192/25-300/25 = -108/25. So DN: (15s', 12-108s'/25, 144s'/25).\n\nB=(15,0,0), M=(375/34, 12, 225/34). Line BM: B + u'(M-B) = (15 + u'(375/34-15), 12u', u'·225/34). 375/34-15 = 375/34-510/34 = -135/34. So BM: (15-135u'/34, 12u', 225u'/34).\n\nSet equal:\n15s' = 15-135u'/34  ... (1')\n12-108s'/25 = 12u'  ... (2')\n144s'/25 = 225u'/34  ... (3')\n\nFrom (3'): s' = 225u'·25/(34·144) = 5625u'/(4896) = 625u'/544. (Same factor as before inverted)\n\nFrom (2'): 12-108s'/25 = 12u' → 12(1-u') = 108s'/25 → 1-u' = 9s'/25 → u' = 1-9s'/25.\n\nSubstitute s' = 625u'/544: u' = 1 - 9·625u'/(25·544) = 1 - 225u'/544... wait 9·625/(25·544) = 5625/13600 = 225/544. So u' = 1 - 225u'/544 → u'(1+225/544) = 1 → u'·769/544 = 1 → u' = 544/769.\n\ns' = 625·544/(544·769) = 625/769.\n\nCheck (1'): 15s' = 15·625/769 = 9375/769. 15-135u'/34 = 15-135·544/(34·769) = 15 - 73440/(34·769) = 15-2160/769 = (15·769-2160)/769 = (11535-2160)/769 = 9375/769. ✓\n\nP: using DN: x = 15·625/769 = 9375/769. y = 12-108·625/(25·769) = 12 - 67500/19225 = 12 - 2700/769 = (12·769-2700)/769 = (9228-2700)/769 = 6528/769. z = 144·625/(25·769) = 90000/19225 = 3600/769.\n\nP = (9375/769, 6528/769, 3600/769).\n\nNow plane (A'AG): A'=(0,0,9), A=(0,0,0), G=(2160/769, 2700/769, 3600/769).\n\nVectors in plane: A→A' = (0,0,9), A→G = (2160/769, 2700/769, 3600/769).\n\nNormal n1 = (0,0,9) × (2160/769, 2700/769, 3600/769) = (0·3600/769 - 9·2700/769, 9·2160/769 - 0, 0-0) = (-24300/769, 19440/769, 0).\n\nSimplify: factor 2430/769: n1 ∝ (-10, 8, 0) → or (-24300, 19440, 0). Divide by 2430: (-10, 8, 0). Or (10, -8, 0) → (5, -4, 0).\n\nSo n1 = (5, -4, 0) (up to sign). Let me verify: (0,0,9)×(2160,2700,3600) = (0·3600-9·2700, 9·2160-0·3600, 0) = (-24300, 19440, 0). Divide by 4860: (-5, 4, 0). So n1 = (-5, 4, 0) or (5, -4, 0).\n\nPlane through A=(0,0,0) with normal (5,-4,0): 5x - 4y = 0.\n\nCheck A': 5·0-4·0=0 ✓. Check G: 5·2160/769 - 4·2700/769 = (10800-10800)/769 = 0 ✓.\n\nPlane (C'CP): C'=(15,12,9), C=(15,12,0), P=(9375/769, 6528/769, 3600/769).\n\nVectors: C→C' = (0,0,9), C→P = (9375/769-15, 6528/769-12, 3600/769) = ((9375-11535)/769, (6528-9228)/769, 3600/769) = (-2160/769, -2700/769, 3600/769).\n\nNormal n2 = (0,0,9) × (-2160/769, -2700/769, 3600/769) = (0·3600/769 - 9·(-2700/769), 9·(-2160/769) - 0, 0) = (24300/769, -19440/769, 0).\n\nSo n2 = (24300, -19440, 0) ∝ (5, -4, 0). Same normal! Good, planes are parallel.\n\nPlane through C=(15,12,0) with normal (5,-4,0): 5(x-15) - 4(y-12) = 0 → 5x - 4y - 75 + 48 = 0 → 5x - 4y - 27 = 0.\n\nSo plane 1: 5x - 4y = 0. Plane 2: 5x - 4y - 27 = 0.\n\nDistance between parallel planes Ax+By+Cz+D1=0 and Ax+By+Cz+D2=0 is |D1-D2|/√(A²+B²+C²).\n\nPlane 1: 5x-4y+0 = 0, D1=0. Plane 2: 5x-4y-27=0, D2=-27.\n\nDistance = |0-(-27)|/√(25+16) = 27/√41.\n\nSo the distance is 27/√41 = 27√41/41.\n\nLet me double check the planes. Plane 1 through A=(0,0,0): 5·0-4·0=0 ✓. Plane 2 through C=(15,12,0): 5·15-4·12 = 75-48 = 27 ✓, so 5x-4y-27=0 gives 27-27=0 ✓.\n\nDistance = 27/√41.\n\nThe answer is 27√41/41, or equivalently 27/√41.\n\nLet me verify G and P computations once more, particularly the cross products and that G lies in plane 5x-4y=0 and P lies in 5x-4y=27.\n\nG = (2160/769, 2700/769, 3600/769): 5·2160 - 4·2700 = 10800-10800 = 0 ✓.\nP = (9375/769, 6528/769, 3600/769): 5·9375 - 4·6528 = 46875 - 26112 = 20763. 20763/769 = 27? 769·27 = 20763. Yes! ✓.\n\nSo the distance between the parallel planes is 27/√41 = 27√41/41.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786684008}
