rallel planes Ax+By+Cz+D1=0 and Ax+By+Cz+D2=0 is |D1-D2|/√(A²+B²+C²).\n\nPlane 1: 5x-4y+0 = 0, D1=0. Plane 2: 5x-4y-27=0, D2=-27.\n\nDistance = |0-(-27)|/√(25+16) = 27/√41.\n\nSo the distance is 27/√41 = 27√41/41.\n\nLet me double check the planes. Plane 1 through A=(0,0,0): 5·0-4·0=0 ✓. Plane 2 through C=(15,12,0): 5·15-4·12 = 75-48 = 27 ✓, so 5x-4y-27=0 gives 27-27=0 ✓.\n\nDistance = 27/√41.\n\nThe answer is 27√41/41, or equivalently 27/√41.\n\nLet me verify G and P computations once more, particularly the cross products and that G lies in plane 5x-4y=0 and P lies in 5x-4y=27.\n\nG = (2160/769, 2700/769, 3600/769): 5·2160 - 4·2700 = 10800-10800 = 0 ✓.\nP = (9375/769, 6528/769, 3600/769): 5·9375 - 4·6528 = 46875 - 26112 = 20763. 20763/769 = 27? 769·27 = 20763. Yes! ✓.\n\nSo the distance between the parallel planes is 27/√41 = 27√41/41.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786684008}
